Why:
- The sample demo completed depth inference but sideview point cloud export failed because unprojection helpers referenced by transform.py were missing.
- The OmegaConf eval resolver printed an error on repeated imports even though the duplicate registration was harmless.

How:
- Added depth_to_cam_coords_points and closed_form_inverse_se3 to transform.py so unproject_depth_map_to_point_map can produce world-space points.
- Reused the same SE3 inverse and camera-coordinate math already present in the Stream3R utility path.
- Changed cfg.py to register the eval resolver only when it is not already registered.
- Verified the demo writes depth maps, raw npz files, pointcloud.ply, and cameras.npz.
